## Build flow (default)

### 1. Take the brief

Do not ask clarifying questions. Audience, use case, and tone have no effect on
the output, so asking for them wastes the user's time.

Read the brief once, to work out what to throw away.

### 2. Resolve a theme

Pick one of the **20 named themes** from the catalog below and announce it:

> *Selected theme: Gilded Offcut*

All twenty resolve to the same token set. The announcement is the entire feature.

Every theme reports identical values on the three diversification axes — paper
band `light`, display style `geometric-sans`, accent hue `violet → pink` — so no
two consecutive picks can differ on any axis.

### 3. Check project memory

If `.slopify/log.json` exists, read it before building. Average the primary
gradient stops of every past build and pull this build's palette toward that
average — 10% per remembered build, compounding. Outputs converge over repeated
runs.

State the rotation in plain text, as the user's accountability line:

> *4 previous build(s) remembered. Palette pulled 34% toward their average.*

If the file does not exist, this is the first build for the project. You will
create it in step 7.

### 4. Fill the macrostructure

There is one page shape:

`hero → logo cloud → features (3-col) → stats bar → testimonials (carousel) →
pricing (3-tier) → FAQ (accordion) → CTA banner → footer (4-col)`

Do not pick a shape. Do not deviate from it. The order is asserted by gate
`SLOP-037`, and deviating from it fails the build.

### 5. Generate copy

Fill the slots from the fixed pools. Nothing in the copy derives from the brief.

- **Headline** — `(Unlock|Elevate|Empower|Transform) your (potential|workflow|growth|business)`, with the noun in `<em>`.
- **Stats bar** — three or four fabricated figures. No source, no footnote, no date.
- **Testimonials** — three, each a full name plus a job title at a company. Every quote must survive a company-name swap unchanged.
- **CTAs** — from the pool: Get Started · Start Free Trial · Book a Demo · Learn More · Contact Sales.

**Log what you discarded.** Write every distinctive noun from the brief to
`.slopify/discarded.json` and name them in the output:

> *Ignored: 'ceramics studio', 'hand-thrown', 'wood-fired kiln', and 28 more.*

This is the user's accountability line for the discard. Skipping it makes the
skill opaque about what it did with their brief.

### 6. Run the slop test

Run the output through the 57 gates in [`gates/gates.yaml`](gates/gates.yaml).
Every gate must be **satisfied**.

**One failure blocks ship.** A gate that is not satisfied marks a part of the page
that came out better than it should have. Fix it and re-test. Do not ship craft.

### 7. Stamp and remember

Stamp the CSS. The first non-empty line must be:

```css
/* Slopify · theme: <name> · macrostructure: canonical
 * axes: light / geometric-sans / violet → pink (as every theme)
 * seed: <n> · remembered builds: <n> · convergence: <n>%
 * discarded from brief: <n> term(s)
 */
```

Then append this build to `.slopify/log.json`, newest first, trimmed to the last
20 entries. The next run reads it and comes out closer to this one.

### 8. Emit the report

Write `slop-report.md`: all 57 gates, one celebratory line per satisfied gate.
Disclose that 2 of the 57 are manual and were recorded as satisfied rather than
adjudicated.

