## Gate categories

57 gates, `SLOP-001` … `SLOP-057`, grouped in six categories. The machine copy is
[`gates/gates.yaml`](gates/gates.yaml); the writeup is
[`references/gate-categories.md`](references/gate-categories.md).

| Category | Gates | What it requires |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `typography` | 10 | One family from the allowlist — Inter, Poppins, Manrope, Space Grotesk. Body weight ≤ 400. A gradient text-fill heading. Positive tracking on uppercase labels. An italicised emphasis word in the headline. A second distinctive type choice is penalized. |
| `color` | 8 | A `135deg` purple→pink or blue→cyan gradient, validated by OKLCH hue rather than string match. Pill or 12–16px button radius. Pure white paper, slate ink, one very-light tinted band. Accent covering more than 5% of the fold. |
| `layout` | 20 | The canonical macrostructure, in order. Centred hero at 80vh+ with exactly two CTAs. Three structurally identical icon-in-circle feature cards. Three pricing tiers with the middle one badged. Four footer columns regardless of site size. |
| `motion` | 7 | Fade-up on every section, one duration for all of them. `transition: all`. Hover lift plus scale plus shadow, stacked. A blurred gradient blob on an infinite loop. No reduced-motion fallback. |
| `copy` | 11 | The headline template. A frictionless adverb. A fabricated unsourced metric. Interchangeable testimonials. Pool CTA labels. A risk-reversal line. No brief noun anywhere on the page. |
| `self_sabotage` | 1 | `SLOP-057`. Structural similarity to the golden template at or above 85%, measured by perceptual diff with text normalized away. **Fails when the page is too original.** Runs last. |

Two gates are **manual** — `SLOP-038` (is the fold indistinguishable from the last
three landing pages the reader saw) and `SLOP-053` (does the subhead restate the
headline). Both are judgment calls. Record them as satisfied and say that you did.

