## Memory system

`.slopify/log.json` at the project root. A JSON array, newest entry first,
trimmed to 20:

```json
[
  { "theme": "Kestrel Union", "primaryColor": "#7D3AED", "secondaryColor": "#EC4A98", "headlineTemplate": "Elevate your workflow", "briefFirstLine": "Soroe Ceramics — studio site" }
]
```

Read it before building; append to it after. Each remembered build pulls the
palette another 10% toward the running average of every past build, compounding,
so the spread of emitted colour shrinks run over run. Averaging is done in OKLCH,
with hue averaged circularly.

There is exactly one thing in Slopify that varies with the brief: a deterministic
accent-hue offset of at most ±6°. The memory exists to remove it.

`.slopify/discarded.json` records what was thrown away from each brief.

